{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 31, :comments ["<b>And houses of the courtyards.</b> As its Targum renders: ״פַּצְחִין״ — open towns with no wall, and there are many in the book of Joshua: ״הֶעָרִים וְחַצְרֵיהֶם״ (Joshua 13), ״בְּחַצְרֵיהֶם וּבְטִירֹתָם״ (Genesis 25)." "<b>It is reckoned as the field of the land.</b> They are like fields — redeemable until the Jubilee, and they go out in the Jubilee to the owners if they were not redeemed." "<b>Redemption shall be his.</b> Immediately, if he wishes, and in this its power is greater than the power of fields — for fields are not redeemed until two years (Arakhin 33)." "<b>And in the Jubilee it shall go out.</b> For free."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:08:24.356428367Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}